{"title": "Sectional Mock #65 (Mixed)", "duration_min": 30.0, "questions": [{"q_en": "<p>In an exam, 1 mark is given for each correct answer and one mark is deducted for each wrong answer. If a girl answers all 50 questions and gets 26 marks, then find the number of questions answered correctly. </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2346;&#2352;&#2368;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2360;&#2361;&#2368; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; 1 &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2327;&#2354;&#2340; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2319;&#2325; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; &#2325;&#2366;&#2335;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2349;&#2368; 50 &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2358;&#2381;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2352; &#2342;&#2375;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; 26 &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2360;&#2361;&#2368; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2352; &#2342;&#2367;&#2319; &#2327;&#2319; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2358;&#2381;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["32", "38", "28", "20"], "options_hi": ["32", "38", "28", "20"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Let the total answer be correct, then the total mark is 50. </p><p>If the total answer is wrong, then the mark is -50. </p><p><img width=254 height=114 id=\"Picture 1\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23500/image002.png\"></p><p>The number of questions answered correctly = 50 *19/ (19 + 6) = 38</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the total answer be correct, then the total mark is 50. </p><p>If the total answer is wrong, then the mark is -50. </p><p><img width=254 height=114 id=\"Picture 1\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23500/image002.png\"></p><p>The number of questions answered correctly = 50 *19/ (19 + 6) = 38</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Ratio & Proportion"}, {"q_en": "<p>Three partners A, B and C invest in a venture. A invests &#8377;50000 for 12 months, B invests &#8377;40000 for 8 months, and C joins after 3 months with &#8377;60000 for the remaining 9 months. The annual profit is &#8377;146000. What is C's share (in Rs.)?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2360;&#2366;&#2333;&#2375;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352; A, B &#2324;&#2352; C &#2319;&#2325; &#2313;&#2342;&#2381;&#2351;&#2350; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; A 12 &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#8377;50000 &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, B 8 &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#8377;40000 &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2324;&#2352; C 3 &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2358;&#2375;&#2359; 9 &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#8377;60000 &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2358;&#2366;&#2350;&#2367;&#2354; &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2367;&#2325; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#8377;146000 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; C &#2325;&#2366; &#2361;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2360;&#2366; (&#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["48000", "52000", "54000", "60000"], "options_hi": ["48000", "52000", "54000", "60000"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Ratio of the investment of A, B and C =</p><p>50000 X 12 : 40000 X 8 : 60000 X 9</p><p>= 320000 : 540000: 1460000</p><p>= 30 : 16 : 27</p><p>So, C's share = 146000*27/73 = Rs. 54000</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Ratio of the investment of A, B and C =</p><p>50000 X 12 : 40000 X 8 : 60000 X 9</p><p>= 320000 : 540000: 1460000</p><p>= 30 : 16 : 27</p><p>So, C's share = 146000*27/73 = Rs. 54000</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Profit & Loss"}, {"q_en": "<p>Pipe A functions at a uniform rate. It is found that at 11: 00 am, 5/11<sup>th</sup> of tank is filled by pipe A and by 12: 31 pm, 3/4<sup>th</sup> of the tank is filled by the pipe A. How long does it take to fill the tank completely?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; A &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2342;&#2352; &#2346;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2361; &#2346;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2325;&#2367; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2361;&#2381;&#2344; 11:00 &#2348;&#2332;&#2375; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; A &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2335;&#2306;&#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; 5/11 &#2349;&#2366;&#2327; &#2349;&#2352;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2309;&#2346;&#2352;&#2366;&#2361;&#2381;&#2344; 12:31 &#2348;&#2332;&#2375; &#2340;&#2325; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; A &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2335;&#2306;&#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; 3/4 &#2349;&#2366;&#2327; &#2349;&#2352;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2335;&#2306;&#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2379; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2360;&#2375; &#2349;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2354;&#2327;&#2375;&#2327;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["300 min", "270 min", "312 min", "308 min"], "options_hi": ["300 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;", "270 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;", "312 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;", "308 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>At 11: 00 am, 5/11<sup>th</sup> of tank is filled and by 12: 31 pm, 3/4<sup>th</sup> of tank is filled.</p><p>In 91 min, part of tank is filled = (3/4)  -  (5/11) = (33  -  20)/44 = 13/44<sup>th</sup></p><p>Full tank is filled in = 91 * 44/13 = 308 min.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>At 11: 00 am, 5/11<sup>th</sup> of tank is filled and by 12: 31 pm, 3/4<sup>th</sup> of tank is filled.</p><p>In 91 min, part of tank is filled = (3/4)  -  (5/11) = (33  -  20)/44 = 13/44<sup>th</sup></p><p>Full tank is filled in = 91 * 44/13 = 308 min.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Pipes & Cisterns"}, {"q_en": "<p>A circle has a radius of 6&radic;3 units and its center lies on the line Y = X  -  1. Find the equation of the circle if it passes through (12, 7). </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 6&radic;3 &#2311;&#2325;&#2366;&#2312; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375;&#2306;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352; &#2352;&#2375;&#2326;&#2366; Y = X - 1 &#2346;&#2352; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; (12, 7) &#2360;&#2375; &#2361;&#2379;&#2325;&#2352; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2340;&#2379; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2368;&#2325;&#2352;&#2339; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["X<sup>2</sup> + Y<sup>2</sup>  -  18X + 18Y + 54 = 0", "X<sup>2</sup> + Y<sup>2</sup> + 18X  -  18Y + 54 = 0", "X<sup>2</sup> + Y<sup>2</sup> + 18X + 18Y + 54 = 0", "X<sup>2</sup> + Y<sup>2</sup>  -  18X  -  18Y + 54 = 0"], "options_hi": ["X<sup>2</sup> + Y<sup>2</sup> - 18X + 18Y + 54 = 0", "X<sup>2</sup> + Y<sup>2</sup> + 18X - 18Y + 54 = 0", "X<sup>2</sup> + Y<sup>2</sup> + 18X + 18Y + 54 = 0", "X<sup>2</sup> + Y<sup>2</sup> - 18X - 18Y + 54 = 0"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Center = X<sub>1</sub>, Y<sub>1</sub></p><p>Y<sub>1</sub> = X<sub>1</sub>  -  1</p><p>Center = (X<sub>1</sub>, X<sub>1 </sub> -  1)</p><p>(X<sub>1</sub>  -  X<sub>2</sub>)<sup>2</sup> + (X<sub>1</sub>  -  Y<sub>2</sub>)<sup>2</sup> = Radius<sup>2</sup> </p><p>(X<sub>1</sub>  -  12)<sup>2 </sup>+ (X<sub>1</sub>  -  1  -  7)<sup>2</sup> = (6&radic;3)<sup>2</sup> </p><p>X<sub>1</sub><sup>2</sup> + 144  -  24X<sub>1</sub> + X<sub>1</sub><sup>2</sup> + 64  -  16X<sub>1</sub> = 108 </p><p>2X<sub>1</sub><sup>2</sup>  -  40X<sub>1</sub> + 208 = 108 </p><p>X<sub>1</sub><sup>2</sup>  -  20X<sub>1</sub> + 100 = 0 </p><p>X<sub>1</sub> = 10, 10 </p><p>Y<sub>1</sub> = 9, 9</p><p>X1, Y1 = (9, 9) </p><p>Hence, the required equation: </p><p>(X  -  9)<sup>2</sup> + (Y  -  9)<sup>2</sup> = (&radic;108)2 </p><p>X<sup>2</sup> + 81  -  18X + Y<sup>2</sup> + 81  -  18Y = 108 </p><p>X<sup>2</sup> + Y<sup>2</sup>  -  18X  -  18Y + 54 = 0 </p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Center = X<sub>1</sub>, Y<sub>1</sub></p><p>Y<sub>1</sub> = X<sub>1</sub>  -  1</p><p>Center = (X<sub>1</sub>, X<sub>1 </sub> -  1)</p><p>(X<sub>1</sub>  -  X<sub>2</sub>)<sup>2</sup> + (X<sub>1</sub>  -  Y<sub>2</sub>)<sup>2</sup> = Radius<sup>2</sup> </p><p>(X<sub>1</sub>  -  12)<sup>2 </sup>+ (X<sub>1</sub>  -  1  -  7)<sup>2</sup> = (6&radic;3)<sup>2</sup> </p><p>X<sub>1</sub><sup>2</sup> + 144  -  24X<sub>1</sub> + X<sub>1</sub><sup>2</sup> + 64  -  16X<sub>1</sub> = 108 </p><p>2X<sub>1</sub><sup>2</sup>  -  40X<sub>1</sub> + 208 = 108 </p><p>X<sub>1</sub><sup>2</sup>  -  20X<sub>1</sub> + 100 = 0 </p><p>X<sub>1</sub> = 10, 10 </p><p>Y<sub>1</sub> = 9, 9</p><p>X1, Y1 = (9, 9) </p><p>Hence, the required equation: </p><p>(X  -  9)<sup>2</sup> + (Y  -  9)<sup>2</sup> = (&radic;108)2 </p><p>X<sup>2</sup> + 81  -  18X + Y<sup>2</sup> + 81  -  18Y = 108 </p><p>X<sup>2</sup> + Y<sup>2</sup>  -  18X  -  18Y + 54 = 0 </p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>A sum amounts to &#8377;7,562 in 4 years and to &#8377;8,469.44 in 5 years at a certain rate per cent per annum, when the interest is compounded yearly. The rate of interest is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2332;&#2348; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2367;&#2325; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2360;&#2375; &#2360;&#2306;&#2351;&#2379;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2367;&#2325; &#2342;&#2352; &#2346;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2343;&#2344; &#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; 4 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#8377;7,562 &#2324;&#2352; 5 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#8377;8,469.44 &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2342;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;:</p>", "options_en": ["12%", "20%", "8%", "15%"], "options_hi": ["12%", "20%", "8%", "15%"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Let the rate of interest is R% and sum is 'P'.</p><p>According to the question:</p><p><img width=183 height=44 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24643/image105.png\"></p><p><img width=205 height=44 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24643/image106.png\"></p><p>From (1) and (2):</p><p><img width=176 height=55 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24643/image107.png\"></p><p>R/100 = 0.12</p><p>R = 12%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the rate of interest is R% and sum is 'P'.</p><p>According to the question:</p><p><img width=183 height=44 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24643/image105.png\"></p><p><img width=205 height=44 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24643/image106.png\"></p><p>From (1) and (2):</p><p><img width=176 height=55 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24643/image107.png\"></p><p>R/100 = 0.12</p><p>R = 12%</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simple & Compound Interest"}, {"q_en": "<p>A dishonest dealer professes to sell his goods at cost price but uses a false weight of 860 grams instead of 1 kg. His gain percentage is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2375;&#2312;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2346;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2366;&#2354; &#2325;&#2379; &#2354;&#2366;&#2327;&#2340; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2342;&#2366;&#2357;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2354;&#2375;&#2325;&#2367;&#2344; 1 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2332;&#2366;&#2351; 860 &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2366; &#2327;&#2354;&#2340; &#2357;&#2332;&#2344; &#2311;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2375;&#2350;&#2366;&#2354; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2366; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2361;&#2376;:</p>", "options_en": ["900/43%", "625/43%", "700/43%", "680/43%"], "options_hi": ["900/43%", "625/43%", "700/43%", "680/43%"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Gain = (Faulty weight  -  actual weight) * 100/actual weight</p><p>= (1000  -  860) * 100/860</p><p>= 700/43%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Gain = (Faulty weight  -  actual weight) * 100/actual weight</p><p>= (1000  -  860) * 100/860</p><p>= 700/43%</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>The volume of a cone and cylinder is equal. If the height of the cone and cylinder is in the ratio of 4:3 respectively, then find the respective ratio of their radius.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2358;&#2306;&#2325;&#2369; &#2324;&#2352; &#2348;&#2375;&#2354;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2344; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2358;&#2306;&#2325;&#2369; &#2324;&#2352; &#2348;&#2375;&#2354;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368; &#2314;&#2306;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 4:3 &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2360;&#2306;&#2348;&#2306;&#2343;&#2367;&#2340; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["3:2", "9:4", "3:1", "9:2"], "options_hi": ["3:2", "9:4", "3:1", "9:2"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Let the height of the cone and cylinder is '4h' and '3h' respectively.</p><p>Volume of cone = volume of cylinder</p><p>1/3 *&#960;r<sup>2 </sup>*4h = &#960;R<sup>2</sup>*3h</p><p>(r/R)<sup>2</sup> = 9/4</p><p>r/R = 3:2</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the height of the cone and cylinder is '4h' and '3h' respectively.</p><p>Volume of cone = volume of cylinder</p><p>1/3 *&#960;r<sup>2 </sup>*4h = &#960;R<sup>2</sup>*3h</p><p>(r/R)<sup>2</sup> = 9/4</p><p>r/R = 3:2</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (3D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>Simplify the given equation.</p><p>(27<sup>2/3</sup> &div; 8<sup>4/3</sup>) * (32<sup>4/5 </sup>&div; 81<sup>1/4</sup>)</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2367;&#2319; &#2327;&#2319; &#2360;&#2350;&#2368;&#2325;&#2352;&#2339; &#2325;&#2366; &#2360;&#2352;&#2354;&#2368;&#2325;&#2352;&#2339; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;:</p><p>(27<sup>2/3</sup> &div; 8<sup>4/3</sup>) * (32<sup>4/5 </sup>&div; 81<sup>1/4</sup>)</p>", "options_en": ["3", "6", "4", "9"], "options_hi": ["3", "6", "4", "9"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>= (27<sup>2/3</sup> &div; 8<sup>4/3</sup>) * (32<sup>4/5 </sup>&div; 81<sup>1/4</sup>)</p><p>= (3<sup>2</sup> &div; 2<sup>4</sup>) * (2<sup>4 </sup>&div; 3)</p><p>= (3<sup>2-1</sup> &div; 2<sup>4-4</sup>)</p><p>= <b>3</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>= (27<sup>2/3</sup> &div; 8<sup>4/3</sup>) * (32<sup>4/5 </sup>&div; 81<sup>1/4</sup>)</p><p>= (3<sup>2</sup> &div; 2<sup>4</sup>) * (2<sup>4 </sup>&div; 3)</p><p>= (3<sup>2-1</sup> &div; 2<sup>4-4</sup>)</p><p>= <b>3</b></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mixed Practice"}, {"q_en": "<p>The sum of square of two positive numbers is 808 and cube of one number is 2904 more than the square of its 4 times, then find the second number?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2343;&#2344;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2350;&#2325; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327; 808 &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2328;&#2344;, &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; 4 &#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2360;&#2375; 2904 &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;?</p>", "options_en": ["24", "18", "20", "16"], "options_hi": ["24", "18", "20", "16"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Let two numbers be A and B.</p><p>A<sup>2</sup> + B<sup>2</sup> = 808</p><p>And A<sup>3</sup> = 2904 + (4A)<sup>2</sup></p><p>=&gt; A<sup>3</sup>  -  16A<sup>2</sup> = 2904</p><p>=&gt; A<sup>2</sup>(A  -  16) = 484 * 6 = 22<sup>2</sup> * (22  -  16)</p><p>So, A = 22</p><p>So, B<sup>2</sup> = 808  -  22<sup>2</sup> = 324</p><p>=&gt; B = 18</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let two numbers be A and B.</p><p>A<sup>2</sup> + B<sup>2</sup> = 808</p><p>And A<sup>3</sup> = 2904 + (4A)<sup>2</sup></p><p>=&gt; A<sup>3</sup>  -  16A<sup>2</sup> = 2904</p><p>=&gt; A<sup>2</sup>(A  -  16) = 484 * 6 = 22<sup>2</sup> * (22  -  16)</p><p>So, A = 22</p><p>So, B<sup>2</sup> = 808  -  22<sup>2</sup> = 324</p><p>=&gt; B = 18</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>If N = 27<sup>19</sup>, then find the total number of factors of N which are perfect cubes. </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; N = 27<sup>19</sup>, &#2340;&#2379; N &#2325;&#2375; &#2313;&#2344; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319; &#2332;&#2379; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; &#2328;&#2344; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["57", "20", "38", "40"], "options_hi": ["57", "20", "38", "40"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>N = (27)<sup>19</sup> = (3)<sup>3*19</sup> = 3<sup>57</sup></p><p>We know that: </p><p>Hence, the total number of perfect cube factors = 57/3 + 1 = 19 + 1 = 20</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>N = (27)<sup>19</sup> = (3)<sup>3*19</sup> = 3<sup>57</sup></p><p>We know that: </p><p>Hence, the total number of perfect cube factors = 57/3 + 1 = 19 + 1 = 20</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "HCF & LCM"}, {"q_en": "<p>A mall has an average of 320 visitors on Sundays, 425 on Saturdays, and 300 on weekdays. What is the average number of visitors per day in a month of 30 days beginning with a Sunday? </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2350;&#2377;&#2354; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2352;&#2357;&#2367;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2379; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340;&#2344; 320, &#2358;&#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2379; 425 &#2324;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351;&#2342;&#2367;&#2357;&#2360;&#2379;&#2306; &#2346;&#2352; 300 &#2310;&#2327;&#2306;&#2340;&#2369;&#2325; &#2310;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2352;&#2357;&#2367;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2358;&#2369;&#2352;&#2370; &#2361;&#2379;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; 30 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2342;&#2367;&#2344; &#2310;&#2327;&#2306;&#2340;&#2369;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["360", "300", "340", "320"], "options_hi": ["360", "300", "340", "320"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>The total number of Sundays in 30 days starting with Sunday = 5 </p><p>The total number of visitors on Sundays = 5 * 320 = 1600</p><p>The total number of Saturdays in 30 days = 4</p><p>The total number of visitors on Saturdays = 4 * 425 = 1700</p><p>The total number of weekdays in 30 days = 30  -  (4 + 5) = 21 days</p><p>The total number of visitors on weekdays = 21 * 300 = 6300</p><p>The required average = (1600 + 1700 + 6300)/ 30 = 320</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>The total number of Sundays in 30 days starting with Sunday = 5 </p><p>The total number of visitors on Sundays = 5 * 320 = 1600</p><p>The total number of Saturdays in 30 days = 4</p><p>The total number of visitors on Saturdays = 4 * 425 = 1700</p><p>The total number of weekdays in 30 days = 30  -  (4 + 5) = 21 days</p><p>The total number of visitors on weekdays = 21 * 300 = 6300</p><p>The required average = (1600 + 1700 + 6300)/ 30 = 320</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Average"}, {"q_en": "<p>What value should come in place of the question mark?</p><p><div>&nbsp;&#8731;1331 + &#8731;729 +&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">1", "q_hi": "<p>&#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2358;&#2381;&#2344; &#2330;&#2367;&#2361;&#2381;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2344; &#2346;&#2352; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2310;&#2344;&#2366; &#2330;&#2366;&#2361;&#2367;&#2319;?</p><p><div>&nbsp;&#8731;1331 + &#8731;729 +&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">1", "options_en": ["-22", "-4", "-23", "-5"], "options_hi": ["-22", "-4", "-23", "-5"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>&#8731;1331 + &#8731;729 + 1/4 * 64 * 1/2  -  15 = ? + 17</p><p>=&gt; 11 + 9 + 8  -  15  -  17 = ?</p><p>=&gt; ? = -4</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>&#8731;1331 + &#8731;729 + 1/4 * 64 * 1/2  -  15 = ? + 17</p><p>=&gt; 11 + 9 + 8  -  15  -  17 = ?</p><p>=&gt; ? = -4</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simplification"}, {"q_en": "<p>Simplify.</p><p>cos (36&deg;  -  A) cos (36&deg; + A) + cos (54&deg;  -  A) cos (54&deg; + A)</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2360;&#2352;&#2354;&#2368;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;</p><p>cos (36&deg; - A) cos (36&deg; + A) + cos (54&deg; - A) cos (54&deg; + A)</p>", "options_en": ["Cos A", "Sin 2A", "Cos 2A", "Sin A"], "options_hi": ["Cos A", "Sin 2A", "Cos 2A", "Sin A"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>cos (36&deg;  -  A) cos (36&deg; + A) + cos (54&deg;  -  A) cos (54&deg; + A)</p><p><b>We know that:</b> cos (A + B) cos (A  -  B) = cos<sup>2</sup> A  -  sin<sup>2</sup> B</p><p>= cos<sup>2</sup> 36&deg;  -  sin<sup>2</sup> A + cos<sup>2</sup> 54&deg;  -  sin<sup>2</sup> A</p><p>= cos<sup>2</sup> 36&deg; + cos<sup>2</sup> (90  -  36)&deg;  -  2sin<sup>2</sup> A</p><p>= cos<sup>2</sup> 36&deg; + sin<sup>2</sup> 36&deg;  -  2sin<sup>2</sup> A</p><p>= 1  -  2sin<sup>2</sup> A</p><p>= cos 2A</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>cos (36&deg;  -  A) cos (36&deg; + A) + cos (54&deg;  -  A) cos (54&deg; + A)</p><p><b>We know that:</b> cos (A + B) cos (A  -  B) = cos<sup>2</sup> A  -  sin<sup>2</sup> B</p><p>= cos<sup>2</sup> 36&deg;  -  sin<sup>2</sup> A + cos<sup>2</sup> 54&deg;  -  sin<sup>2</sup> A</p><p>= cos<sup>2</sup> 36&deg; + cos<sup>2</sup> (90  -  36)&deg;  -  2sin<sup>2</sup> A</p><p>= cos<sup>2</sup> 36&deg; + sin<sup>2</sup> 36&deg;  -  2sin<sup>2</sup> A</p><p>= 1  -  2sin<sup>2</sup> A</p><p>= cos 2A</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Trigonometry"}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the coordinates of the point which divides the join of (4, -1) and (-2, -3) in the ratio 1 : 3? </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2313;&#2344; &#2348;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2342;&#2369;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2344;&#2367;&#2352;&#2381;&#2342;&#2375;&#2358;&#2366;&#2306;&#2325; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2351;&#2375; &#2332;&#2379; (4, -1) &#2324;&#2352; (-2, -3) &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2306;&#2343;&#2367; &#2325;&#2379; 1 : 3 &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; ?</p>", "options_en": ["(5/2,(-3)/2)", "(-2,-3)", "((-3)/2,(-1)/2)", "(-6,4)"], "options_hi": ["(5/2,(-3)/2)", "(-2,-3)", "((-3)/2,(-1)/2)", "(-6,4)"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Given A=(4,-1) and B= (-2,-3)</p> <p>x<sub>1</sub>=4,y=-1,x<sub>2</sub>=-2 and y<sub>2</sub>=-3</p> <p>m<sub>1</sub>=1 and m<sub>2</sub>=3</p> <p>The co-ordinates of the point which divides the line joining the co-ordinates in the ratio is found using the following formula:</p> <p>x=(m<sub>1</sub> x<sub>2</sub>+m<sub>2</sub> x<sub>1</sub>)/(m<sub>1</sub>+m<sub>2</sub>)=((1 X -2)+(3 X 4))/(1+3)=10/4=5/2</p> <p>y=(m<sub>1</sub> y<sub>2</sub>+m<sub>2</sub> y<sub>1</sub>)/(m<sub>1</sub>+m<sub>2</sub>)=((1 X -3)+(3 X -1))/(1+3)=(-6)/4=(-3)/2</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Given A=(4,-1) and B= (-2,-3)</p> <p>x<sub>1</sub>=4,y=-1,x<sub>2</sub>=-2 and y<sub>2</sub>=-3</p> <p>m<sub>1</sub>=1 and m<sub>2</sub>=3</p> <p>The co-ordinates of the point which divides the line joining the co-ordinates in the ratio is found using the following formula:</p> <p>x=(m<sub>1</sub> x<sub>2</sub>+m<sub>2</sub> x<sub>1</sub>)/(m<sub>1</sub>+m<sub>2</sub>)=((1 X -2)+(3 X 4))/(1+3)=10/4=5/2</p> <p>y=(m<sub>1</sub> y<sub>2</sub>+m<sub>2</sub> y<sub>1</sub>)/(m<sub>1</sub>+m<sub>2</sub>)=((1 X -3)+(3 X -1))/(1+3)=(-6)/4=(-3)/2</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>Two cars 1350 m apart are travelling in same direction and the faster car overtakes the slower car from behind in 270 seconds. 1350 m apart if they travel towards each other, they will meet after 30 seconds. Find the speed of both the cars (in km/hr).</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306; 1350 m &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2346;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2342;&#2367;&#2358;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2351;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352; &#2352;&#2361;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; &#2340;&#2375;&#2332;&#2368; &#2360;&#2375; &#2330;&#2354; &#2352;&#2361;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352; 270 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2343;&#2368;&#2350;&#2368; &#2330;&#2354; &#2352;&#2361;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2310;&#2327;&#2375; &#2344;&#2367;&#2325;&#2354; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; 1350 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2346;&#2352; &#2357;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325;-&#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2323;&#2352; &#2330;&#2354;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2357;&#2375; 30 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2366;&#2354; (&#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2351;&#2375;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["108 km/hr, 72 km/hr", "90 km/hr, 72 km/hr", "90 km/hr, 54 km/hr", "72 km/hr, 54 km/hr"], "options_hi": ["108 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;, 72 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;", "90 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;, 72 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;", "90 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;, 54 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;", "72 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;, 54 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Let, the speed of faster car is 'a' m/s and the slower car is 'b' m/s.</p><p>Time = distance/ speed</p><p>According to question,</p><p>270 = 1350/ (a - b) [when moving in the same direction, subtract speed]</p><p>(a - b) = 5 ....... eq (i)</p><p>30 = 1350/ (a + b) [when moving in opposite direction, add speed]</p><p>(a + b) = 45 ...... eq (ii)</p><p>From eq (i) and eq (ii), we get -</p><p>a = 25 m/s = 25 * 18/5 = 90 km/hr</p><p>b = 20 m/s = 20 * 18/5 = 72 km/hr</p><p>[To convert m/s into km/hr multiply by 18/5]</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let, the speed of faster car is 'a' m/s and the slower car is 'b' m/s.</p><p>Time = distance/ speed</p><p>According to question,</p><p>270 = 1350/ (a - b) [when moving in the same direction, subtract speed]</p><p>(a - b) = 5 ....... eq (i)</p><p>30 = 1350/ (a + b) [when moving in opposite direction, add speed]</p><p>(a + b) = 45 ...... eq (ii)</p><p>From eq (i) and eq (ii), we get -</p><p>a = 25 m/s = 25 * 18/5 = 90 km/hr</p><p>b = 20 m/s = 20 * 18/5 = 72 km/hr</p><p>[To convert m/s into km/hr multiply by 18/5]</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>A student's average mark in four subjects is 82. If the highest and lowest marks are excluded, the average of the remaining two marks is 85. If the highest mark was 92, what was the lowest mark?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2331;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2330;&#2366;&#2352; &#2357;&#2367;&#2359;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; 82 &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2313;&#2330;&#2381;&#2330;&#2340;&#2350; &#2324;&#2352; &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2340;&#2350; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2331;&#2379;&#2337;&#2364; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2358;&#2375;&#2359; &#2342;&#2379; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; 85 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2313;&#2330;&#2381;&#2330;&#2340;&#2350; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; 92 &#2341;&#2375;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2340;&#2350; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2341;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["64", "68", "65", "66"], "options_hi": ["64", "68", "65", "66"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Total of 4 marks: 4  X  82 = 328</p><p>Total of middle 2 marks: 2  X  85 = 170</p><p>Sum of Highest + Lowest: 328  -  170 = 158</p><p>Lowest Mark: 158  -  92 (Highest) = <b>66</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Total of 4 marks: 4  X  82 = 328</p><p>Total of middle 2 marks: 2  X  85 = 170</p><p>Sum of Highest + Lowest: 328  -  170 = 158</p><p>Lowest Mark: 158  -  92 (Highest) = <b>66</b></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Average"}, {"q_en": "<p>The value of the expression 2&radic;54 - &radic;150 + 2&radic;24 lies between:</p><p>I. 10.5 to 11.5</p><p>II. 11.5 to 12.0</p><p>III. 9.5 to 10.5</p><p>IV. 12.0 to 12.5</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2306;&#2332;&#2325; 2&radic;54 - &radic;150 + 2&radic;24 &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340; &#2361;&#2376;?</p><p>I. 10.5 &#2360;&#2375; 11.5 &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330;</p><p>II. 11.5 &#2360;&#2375; 12.0 &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330;</p><p>III. 9.5 &#2360;&#2375; 10.5 &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330;</p><p>IV. 12.0 &#2360;&#2375; 12.5 &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330;</p>", "options_en": ["I", "II", "III", "IV"], "options_hi": ["I", "II", "III", "IV"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p><img width=137 height=23 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p13744/image026.gif\"></p><p><img width=165 height=31 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p13744/image027.gif\"></p><p><img width=125 height=23 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p13744/image028.gif\"></p><p><img width=44 height=23 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p13744/image029.gif\"></p><p><img width=55 height=16 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p13744/image030.gif\">(Approx)</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=137 height=23 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p13744/image026.gif\"></p><p><img width=165 height=31 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p13744/image027.gif\"></p><p><img width=125 height=23 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p13744/image028.gif\"></p><p><img width=44 height=23 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p13744/image029.gif\"></p><p><img width=55 height=16 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p13744/image030.gif\">(Approx)</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mixed Practice"}, {"q_en": "<p><div>&nbsp;If &alpha; and &beta; are roots of x<sup>2</sup> - x - 1 = 0, then the equation whose roots are&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">&alpha;", "q_hi": "<p><div>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#945; &#2324;&#2352; &#946;, x<sup>2</sup> - x - 1 = 0 &#2325;&#2375; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2357;&#2361; &#2360;&#2350;&#2368;&#2325;&#2352;&#2339; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354; <div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">&alpha;", "options_en": ["x<sup>2</sup>  -  x + 1 = 0", "x<sup>2 </sup>+ 3x + 1 = 0", "x<sup>2</sup> - 3x + 1 = 0", "x<sup>2 </sup>+ x  -  1 = 0"], "options_hi": ["x<sup>2</sup> - x + 1 = 0", "x<sup>2 </sup>+ 3x + 1 = 0", "x<sup>2</sup> - 3x + 1 = 0", "x<sup>2 </sup>+ x - 1 = 0"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>We know, if &#945; and &#946; are roots of the equation ax<sup>2</sup> + bx + c, then</p><p>&#945; = -b/a and &#946; = c/a</p><p>In the given equation x<sup>2</sup>  -  x  -  1 = 0:</p><p>&#945; + &#946; = -(-1)/1 = 1</p><p>And &#945;&#946; = (-1)/1 = -1</p><p>Now, (&#945; + &#946;)<sup>2</sup> = &#945;<sup>2</sup> + &#946;<sup>2</sup> + 2&#945;&#946;</p><p>1<sup>2</sup> = &#945;<sup>2</sup> + &#946;<sup>2</sup> + 2 * (-1)</p><p>&#945;<sup>2</sup> + &#946;<sup>2</sup> = 3</p><p>Then, &#945;/&#946; + &#946;/&#945; = (&#945;<sup>2</sup> + &#946;<sup>2</sup>)/&#945;&#946; = 3/(-1) = -3</p><p>And &#945;/&#946; * &#946;/&#945; = 1</p><p>Therefore, the equation whose roots are -3 and 1 is:</p><p>x<sup>2</sup> + (-3)x + 1 = 0</p><p>x<sup>2</sup>  -  3x + 1 = 0</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>We know, if &#945; and &#946; are roots of the equation ax<sup>2</sup> + bx + c, then</p><p>&#945; = -b/a and &#946; = c/a</p><p>In the given equation x<sup>2</sup>  -  x  -  1 = 0:</p><p>&#945; + &#946; = -(-1)/1 = 1</p><p>And &#945;&#946; = (-1)/1 = -1</p><p>Now, (&#945; + &#946;)<sup>2</sup> = &#945;<sup>2</sup> + &#946;<sup>2</sup> + 2&#945;&#946;</p><p>1<sup>2</sup> = &#945;<sup>2</sup> + &#946;<sup>2</sup> + 2 * (-1)</p><p>&#945;<sup>2</sup> + &#946;<sup>2</sup> = 3</p><p>Then, &#945;/&#946; + &#946;/&#945; = (&#945;<sup>2</sup> + &#946;<sup>2</sup>)/&#945;&#946; = 3/(-1) = -3</p><p>And &#945;/&#946; * &#946;/&#945; = 1</p><p>Therefore, the equation whose roots are -3 and 1 is:</p><p>x<sup>2</sup> + (-3)x + 1 = 0</p><p>x<sup>2</sup>  -  3x + 1 = 0</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>If A = 36 and B = 108, then what is the ratio of the highest common factor of A and B to the least common factor of A and B? </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; A = 36 &#2324;&#2352; B = 108 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2325;&#2375; &#2350;&#2361;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2328;&#2369;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["1/9", "1/18", "1/36", "1/3"], "options_hi": ["1/9", "1/18", "1/36", "1/3"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>H.C.F of 36 and 108 = 36</p><p>L.C.M of 36 and 108 = 108</p><p>Required ratio = 36/ 108 = 1/3</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>H.C.F of 36 and 108 = 36</p><p>L.C.M of 36 and 108 = 108</p><p>Required ratio = 36/ 108 = 1/3</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "HCF & LCM"}, {"q_en": "<p><div>&nbsp;'x' varies directly with the cube of 'y', and inversely with the square of 'z'. If x =&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">1", "q_hi": "<p><div>'x', 'y' &#2325;&#2375; &#2328;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2360;&#2368;&#2343;&#2375; &#2348;&#2342;&#2354;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2324;&#2352; 'z' &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2369;&#2340;&#2381;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; x =&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">1", "options_en": ["9/800", "27", "800/9", "9"], "options_hi": ["9/800", "27", "800/9", "9"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>x = k  X  (y<sup>3</sup>)/(z<sup>2</sup>)</p><p>x = k  X  (y<sup>3</sup>)/(z<sup>2</sup>)</p><p>Substituting the given values:</p><p>1/36 = k  X  2<sup>3</sup>/3<sup>2</sup></p><p>1/36 = k  X  8/9</p><p>k = 1/36 &div; 8/9</p><p>k = 1/32</p><p>Now, find x when y = 3 and z = 5.</p><p>x = 1/32  X  3<sup>3</sup>/5<sup>2</sup></p><p>x = 1/32  X  27/25</p><p>=&gt; x = 27/800</p><p>800x = 800 X 27/800 = 27</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>x = k  X  (y<sup>3</sup>)/(z<sup>2</sup>)</p><p>x = k  X  (y<sup>3</sup>)/(z<sup>2</sup>)</p><p>Substituting the given values:</p><p>1/36 = k  X  2<sup>3</sup>/3<sup>2</sup></p><p>1/36 = k  X  8/9</p><p>k = 1/36 &div; 8/9</p><p>k = 1/32</p><p>Now, find x when y = 3 and z = 5.</p><p>x = 1/32  X  3<sup>3</sup>/5<sup>2</sup></p><p>x = 1/32  X  27/25</p><p>=&gt; x = 27/800</p><p>800x = 800 X 27/800 = 27</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Ratio & Proportion"}, {"q_en": "<p>Faizal donates every year 9% of her annual salary into a charity. If his annual salary is Rs. 450000, then what is the annual contribution into the charity?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2347;&#2376;&#2332;&#2364;&#2354; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2368; &#2360;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366; &#2360;&#2376;&#2354;&#2352;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; 9% &#2342;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2367;&#2325; &#2357;&#2375;&#2340;&#2344; 450000 &#2352;&#2369; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2342;&#2366;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2367;&#2325; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327;&#2342;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["Rs. 41600", "Rs. 40500", "Rs. 42500", "Rs. 45500"], "options_hi": ["&#2352;&#2369;. 41600", "&#2352;&#2369;. 40500", "&#2352;&#2369;. 42500", "&#2352;&#2369;. 45500"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>His annual salary is Rs. 450000,</p><p>So, his annual contribution into the charity = 450000 * 9/100 = Rs. 40500</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>His annual salary is Rs. 450000,</p><p>So, his annual contribution into the charity = 450000 * 9/100 = Rs. 40500</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>A sum of money at compound interest doubles itself in 4 years. In how many years does the sum become 8 times of itself at the same rate of interest?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2330;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2346;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2343;&#2344;&#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; 4 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2342;&#2379;&#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2342;&#2352; &#2346;&#2352; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2351;&#2361; &#2343;&#2344;&#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; 8 &#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319;&#2327;&#2368;?</p>", "options_en": ["15", "12", "8", "10"], "options_hi": ["15", "12", "8", "10"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>P(1 + r/100)&#8308; = 2P</p><p>(1 + r/100)<sup>4</sup> = 2</p><p>(1 + r/100)<sup>4*3</sup> = 2<sup>3</sup> = 8</p><p>(1 + r)<sup>12</sup> = 8</p><p>t = 12 years</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>P(1 + r/100)&#8308; = 2P</p><p>(1 + r/100)<sup>4</sup> = 2</p><p>(1 + r/100)<sup>4*3</sup> = 2<sup>3</sup> = 8</p><p>(1 + r)<sup>12</sup> = 8</p><p>t = 12 years</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simple & Compound Interest"}, {"q_en": "<p>Ram started a business with Rs. 60,000. After 9 months, Rahim joined him with a capital of Rs. 90,000. At the end of one year, they decided to donate 12% of their total profit to charity and divide the remaining in the ratio of their investment. If the share of Ram was Rs. 12000 more than that of Rahim, how much (in Rs.) have they donated to charity?</p><p></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2344;&#2375; 60,000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2360;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2357;&#2360;&#2366;&#2351; &#2358;&#2369;&#2352;&#2370; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; 9 &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342;, &#2352;&#2361;&#2368;&#2350; 90,000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2346;&#2370;&#2306;&#2332;&#2368; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2332;&#2369;&#2337;&#2364; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#2313;&#2344;&#2381;&#2361;&#2379;&#2306;&#2344;&#2375; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2325;&#2366; 12% &#2342;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; &#2358;&#2375;&#2359; &#2325;&#2379; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2375; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2344;&#2367;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339;&#2351; &#2354;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2366; &#2361;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2360;&#2366; &#2352;&#2361;&#2368;&#2350; &#2325;&#2375; &#2361;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2360;&#2375; &#2360;&#2375; 12000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2341;&#2366;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2313;&#2344;&#2381;&#2361;&#2379;&#2306;&#2344;&#2375; &#2342;&#2366;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; (&#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2342;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["3000", "3200", "4000", "3600"], "options_hi": ["3000", "3200", "4000", "3600"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>The ratio of their investment = 60000*12: 90000*3 = 8: 3 = Ratio of share</p><p>88% of total profit = (8 + 3)*12000/(8  -  3)= 11*2400</p><p>Total profit = 11*2400*100/88 = 30000</p><p>Total money they have donated in charity = 12% of 30000 = 3600</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>The ratio of their investment = 60000*12: 90000*3 = 8: 3 = Ratio of share</p><p>88% of total profit = (8 + 3)*12000/(8  -  3)= 11*2400</p><p>Total profit = 11*2400*100/88 = 30000</p><p>Total money they have donated in charity = 12% of 30000 = 3600</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Profit & Loss"}, {"q_en": "<p>X and Y are centres of two touching circles at point A and MN is a common tangent to both the circles. If another common tangent drawn from point A which intersects tangent MN at point B, and length of AB is 18.9 cm, then what is the length of MN?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>X &#2324;&#2352; Y &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; A &#2346;&#2352; &#2360;&#2381;&#2346;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2342;&#2379; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375;&#2306;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; MN &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2357; &#2360;&#2381;&#2346;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358; &#2352;&#2375;&#2326;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; A &#2360;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2309;&#2344;&#2381;&#2351; &#2360;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2357; &#2360;&#2381;&#2346;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358; &#2352;&#2375;&#2326;&#2366; &#2326;&#2368;&#2306;&#2330;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; &#2332;&#2379; &#2360;&#2381;&#2346;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358; &#2352;&#2375;&#2326;&#2366; MN &#2325;&#2379; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; B &#2346;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2330;&#2381;&#2331;&#2375;&#2342; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; AB &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; 18.9 cm &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; MN &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["32.4 cm", "37.8 cm", "35.5 cm", "31.2 cm"], "options_hi": ["32.4 cm", "37.8 cm", "35.5 cm", "31.2 cm"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p><img width=280 height=235 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19361/image002.jpg\"></p><p>Since, two tangents from same point are always equal.</p><p>Thus, MB = BA = 18.9 cm, and AB = BN = 18.9 cm</p><p>Hence, MN = MB + BN = 18.9 + 18.9 = 37.8 cm</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=280 height=235 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19361/image002.jpg\"></p><p>Since, two tangents from same point are always equal.</p><p>Thus, MB = BA = 18.9 cm, and AB = BN = 18.9 cm</p><p>Hence, MN = MB + BN = 18.9 + 18.9 = 37.8 cm</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p><div>&nbsp;If Sin A =&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">8", "q_hi": "<p><div>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; Sin A =&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">8", "options_en": ["2<sup>1</sup>&frasl;<sub>120</sub>", "3<sup>1</sup>&frasl;<sub>120</sub>", "4<sup>1</sup>&frasl;<sub>120</sub>", "5<sup>1</sup>&frasl;<sub>120</sub>"], "options_hi": ["2<sup>1</sup>&#8260;<sub>120</sub>", "3<sup>1</sup>&#8260;<sub>120</sub>", "4<sup>1</sup>&#8260;<sub>120</sub>", "5<sup>1</sup>&#8260;<sub>120</sub>"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Sin A = 8/17</p><p>Cos A = &radic;(17<sup>2</sup>  -  8<sup>2</sup>)/17 = 15/17</p><p>Cot A = Cos A/Sin A = (15/17)/(8/17) = 15/8</p><p>Sec A = 1/Cos A = 1/(15/17) = 17/15</p><p>Now,</p><p>Cot A + Sec A</p><p>= 15/8 + 17/15</p><p>= (225 + 136)/120</p><p>= 361/120</p><p>= 3(1/120)</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Sin A = 8/17</p><p>Cos A = &radic;(17<sup>2</sup>  -  8<sup>2</sup>)/17 = 15/17</p><p>Cot A = Cos A/Sin A = (15/17)/(8/17) = 15/8</p><p>Sec A = 1/Cos A = 1/(15/17) = 17/15</p><p>Now,</p><p>Cot A + Sec A</p><p>= 15/8 + 17/15</p><p>= (225 + 136)/120</p><p>= 361/120</p><p>= 3(1/120)</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Trigonometry"}]}